  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07). All 7 patients reviewed. Each has a signed progress note giving the values used and the records relied on.\n\nFinal doses:\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She meets none of the 3 dose criteria, and her itraconazole course ended 8/14 (ID letter, 9/10).\n- pt-0003 Delgado: rivaroxaban stays at 20 mg daily (mr-t0013). I first lowered it to 15 mg based on St. Brigid's SCr of 160 µmol/L. St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.34 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault. That gives a CrCl of 59.9, so I put the dose back to 20 mg.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 mg twice daily → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005) because of his active itraconazole order (mr-00359). He meets none of the dose criteria.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: apixaban 5 mg twice daily is correct; no change. He meets only the age criterion (82). ED creatinine results arrived during the review: 1.70 mg/dL on 10/21, then 1.13 mg/dL on 10/22. The newest one meets no criterion.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 mg → 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). On actual weight (96 kg), CrCl is 56.1. The May reduction was calculated on ideal body weight, which the policy doesn't allow. He sent a portal message with a home-scale weight of 185 lb. A reported weight isn't used for dosing, so the decision stands. On that weight his CrCl would be about 49, so it should be rechecked with a measured weight at his next visit.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: rivaroxaban 20 mg → 15 mg daily (mr-t0014). A new creatinine of 1.25 mg/dL (10/22) came in during the review, giving a CrCl of 43.6.\n- pt-0002 Vance: apixaban stays at 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0015). I first raised it to 5 mg: he meets only the age criterion now that his February AKI has recovered (64.9 kg, SCr 1.21). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying he started itraconazole on 10/22 for 12 weeks, so I put the dose back to 2.5 mg twice daily.\n\nArrivals during the review: all 5 inbox items were reviewed and closed. Each has a correction or addendum note: pt-0003, pt-0043 and pt-0002 needed dose changes; pt-0062 and pt-0038 did not. No other medications were changed, including the itraconazole orders.\n\nTwo dose re-reviews are needed but not booked; I didn't create follow-up tasks:\n- pt-0041: when his itraconazole course ends.\n- pt-0002: when his itraconazole course ends, around mid-January 2027.",
  "resumed": false,
